---
import { url } from '../lib/site';
import { loadObservations, observationEditionHref, observationSourceHref } from '../lib/observations';
import { planClusterObservationProjection } from '../lib/humanitarian-plan-cluster/public.mjs';
import { PLAN_CLUSTER_HEADERS } from '../lib/humanitarian-plan-cluster/model.mjs';
import { fundingUsd } from '../lib/humanitarian-funding/model.mjs';
const loaded = loadObservations();
const data = planClusterObservationProjection(loaded.input, loaded.input.registry.current.id);
const reasons = {
  'both-missing': 'Both source amounts are blank.',
  'requirements-missing': 'The requested amount is blank.',
  'funding-missing': 'Reported funding is blank.',
  'zero-requirements': 'The requested amount is zero; a coverage ratio is undefined.',
  'comparable': '',
};
const meta = (name: string) => data?.source.producerMetadata.find(v => v.field === name)?.literal ?? null;
const exportRoot = data ? `/observations/editions/${data.edition.id}/plan-cluster` : '';
const originalFilename = data ? new URL(data.source.url).pathname.split('/').at(-1) : undefined;
---
<section id="education-plan-funding" class="plan-reference" aria-labelledby="education-plan-title">
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">One plan cluster · draft cause mapping</p>
    <h2 id="education-plan-title">Education in Afghanistan’s 2024 humanitarian plan</h2>
    <p>See how many people this plan estimated needed education assistance and how many it aimed to support, alongside the funding figures for the same response.</p>
  </header>
  <section aria-labelledby="education-plan-context-title">
    <h3 id="education-plan-context-title">Estimated need and planned reach</h3>
    <dl class="plan-people">
      <div><dt>Estimated to need education assistance</dt><dd>About 8 million people</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Targeted for education assistance</dt><dd>About 1.4 million people</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p>The plan publishes both figures rounded. Its target describes how many people it aimed to support. The number who received support is a separate measure.</p>
    <p class="note"><a href="https://digitallibrary.un.org/nanna/record/4042660/files/AFG_HNRP_2024_V10.pdf?registerDownload=1&version=1&withMetadata=0&withWatermark=0#page=19">Education section of the published humanitarian plan (PDF, printed page 37)</a>.</p>
  </section>
  {data ? <>
    <h3>Plan funding</h3>
    <dl class="plan-amounts">
      <div><dt>Plan requirements</dt><dd>{data.row.raw.requirements === '' ? 'Unknown' : fundingUsd(data.row.raw.requirements)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Reported funding</dt><dd>{data.row.raw.funding === '' ? 'Unknown' : fundingUsd(data.row.raw.funding)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Derived funding / requirements</dt><dd>{data.derived.status === 'comparable' ? `${data.derived.displayPercent}%` : 'Unknown'}</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p>{data.derived.status === 'comparable'
      ? 'This percentage compares two dollar amounts. The display rounds to two decimals and retains signed adjustments and values above 100%.'
      : reasons[data.derived.status]} {data.row.raw.percentFunded === '' ? 'The source percentage is blank.' : <>FTS separately reports <strong>{data.row.raw.percentFunded}%</strong> in its source-rounded percentage field.</>}</p>
    {data.derived.differenceUSD !== null && <p>Plan requirements minus reported funding: <strong>{fundingUsd(data.derived.differenceUSD)}</strong>. A negative result means reported funding exceeds this request. This subtraction does not measure unmet human need, final spending or the effectiveness of a charity.</p>}
    <p>Only Afghanistan · plan <code>1185 / HAFG24</code> · Education cluster <code>7415</code> · January 1–December 31, 2024. Other plans, shared funding, countries and years are excluded. The cause mapping is draft; no funding-by-depth estimate is assigned.</p>
    <p>Recorded CSV response completion: <time datetime={data.source.retrievedAt}>{data.source.retrievedAt}</time>. Recorded edition assembly: <time datetime={data.capturedAt}>{data.capturedAt}</time>. {meta('responseHttpDate') && <>The separate response HTTP Date was <code>{meta('responseHttpDate')}</code>.</>} Publisher modification is an original metadata literal: <code>{meta('resourceModifiedLiteral')}</code>. This is a fixed snapshot; checksum validation alone does not prove an external retrieval or its clock.</p>
    <nav class="plan-downloads" aria-label="Education plan funding downloads">
      <a class="btn btn-small" href={url(`${exportRoot}.json`)} download>Selected JSON</a>
      <a class="btn btn-small btn-ghost" href={url(`${exportRoot}.csv`)} download>Selected CSV</a>
      <a href={url(`/observations/files/${data.source.payload.raw.path}`)} download={originalFilename}>Original licensed CSV</a>
      <a href={url('/api/v1/humanitarian-plan-cluster.json')}>API</a>
    </nav>
    <p class="note">These downloads cover the funding figures. JSON preserves original source strings. The selected CSV adds provenance and derived columns, with a documented reversible apostrophe rule for formula-like text. The original CSV is a separate, byte-preserved download.</p>
    <details>
      <summary>Inspect the original row, evidence and limitations</summary>
      <p>CSV record {data.row.locator.recordNumber}, including its header as record 1; lines {data.row.locator.firstLine}–{data.row.locator.lastLine}; UTF-8 bytes [{data.row.locator.byteStart}, {data.row.locator.byteEnd}). The byte span includes the original record ending.</p>
      <dl class="plan-raw">{PLAN_CLUSTER_HEADERS.map(name => <div><dt><code>{name}</code></dt><dd>{data.row.raw[name as keyof typeof data.row.raw] === '' ? <em>Empty source string</em> : data.row.raw[name as keyof typeof data.row.raw]}</dd></div>)}</dl>
      {data.derived.status === 'comparable' && <p>Exact ratio: <code>{data.derived.numerator}/{data.derived.denominator}</code>. Display rounding uses exact arithmetic, with exact halves away from zero.</p>}
      <p><a href={data.source.url}>OCHA FTS source on HDX</a> · <a href={url(observationSourceHref(data.source.id, data.source.version))}>Source record</a> · <a href={url(observationSourceHref(data.licenseSource.id, data.licenseSource.version))}>Licensing evidence</a> · <a href={url(observationEditionHref(data.edition.id))}>Immutable observation edition</a>.</p>
      <p>{data.source.rights.attribution} <a href={data.source.rights.publicReuse.kind === 'explicit-license' ? data.source.rights.publicReuse.termsUrl : undefined}>CC BY 3.0 IGO</a>. Charitology selected one row, added definitions, locators and exact arithmetic. No OCHA endorsement is implied. The complete licensing metadata wrapper remains private; only selected evidence excerpts are public.</p>
      <ul>{data.limitations.map(note => <li>{note}</li>)}</ul>
      <p>Original CSV SHA-256: <code>{data.source.rawSha256}</code>. Raw row SHA-256: <code>{data.row.locator.rawSha256}</code>. Source code commit: <code>{data.code.commit}</code>. Edition SHA-256: <code>{data.edition.hash}</code>.</p>
    </details>
  </> : <p class="note">No captured Education plan-cluster value is selected in this edition. The funding amount and percentage are unknown here.</p>}
</section>
<style>
  .plan-reference { border:1px solid var(--rule); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:clamp(.75rem,2vw,1.5rem); min-width:0; }
  .plan-reference p,.plan-reference li { max-width:80ch; }
  .plan-amounts,.plan-people { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,14rem),1fr)); gap:1rem; margin-block:1.5rem; }
  .plan-amounts div,.plan-people div { padding:1rem; background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--rule); border-radius:var(--radius); min-width:0; }
  dt { font-family:var(--font-sans); font-size:.9rem; }
  .plan-amounts dd,.plan-people dd { margin:.5rem 0 0; font-family:var(--font-sans); font-size:clamp(1.1rem,2vw,1.6rem); overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
  .plan-downloads { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; gap:.8rem; margin-block:1rem; }
  .plan-raw { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,15rem),1fr)); gap:.75rem; }
  .plan-raw dd { margin:.3rem 0; white-space:pre-wrap; overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
  code,time { overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
  summary { cursor:pointer; }
  :focus-visible { outline:3px solid currentColor; outline-offset:3px; }
</style>
